WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.880
Memory loss can interrupt an ordinary morning.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.160
The difficult moment is not always forgetting a name.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.320
Sometimes, it is forgetting what comes next.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.420
In this fictional example, Meera planned to make tea, then water

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.020
her plant.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.740
A phone call interrupted her.

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:18.260
Now she asks, “What was I doing?”

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.740
Threadline connects her saved words with the current camera view.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.720
The blue mug is still empty.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.660
Her earlier conversation supplies the missing plan.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.600
The camera alone cannot know her intention.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.560
A transcript alone cannot show what is in front of her

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:32.940
now.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.540
The agent can say, “You were making tea.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.720
Let’s finish that first,” and show the evidence behind it.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.720
It can also recall where she left her glasses, and draft

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.260
a caregiver note for her approval.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.440
This is a prototype for everyday memory support.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.900
It does not diagnose dementia or confirm task completion.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.180
Less searching.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.000
One clear next step.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.940
More confidence to carry on.
